    "content": { "title": null, "text": "Someone bought your product, took a better photo of it than your last shoot, and posted it. \n\nIt's sitting there right now with 200 likes.\n\nYou can't use it. Not until they say you can.\n\nSo most teams do it the slow way. Open the post, slide into the DMs, type the message, wait. Then do it again. And again. \n\nForty times. By the time the replies come back the campaign has shipped without them.\n\nThat's the part Taggbox takes off your plate.\n\nYou pick the posts you want. One click sends every rights request together, each one carrying your logo and your terms so people know it's real and actually reply. \n\nWhen someone approves, it's logged against that post with the date, so nobody in legal is chasing anyone. And you get the original file, not a screenshot lifted off the feed.\n\nThe photo was always good. Now you're allowed to use it.\nSwipe through →" },
